where will i store the qsns?

You will store your live mock question files inside a dedicated folder named livemock located right in the root directory of your project (the same level where your quizzes/, notes/, and descriptive/ folders are).
Step-by-Step Guide:

    Create the Folder: In your project's root directory, create a new folder named livemock. (If it doesn't exist, the helper function in server.js will automatically create it when you start a quiz, but creating it manually is best).

    Add JSON Files: Inside the livemock/ folder, save your test files as JSON files named after their Test ID. For example, if you want your Test ID to be mock1, create a file named mock1.json.

Example File Structure:

Your file structure should look like this:
Plaintext

your-project-root/
│
├── quizzes/              <-- Normal mock tests
├── notes/                <-- Study notes
├── descriptive/          <-- Descriptive worksheets
├── livemock/             <-- NEW: Live mock tests folder
│   └── mock1.json        <-- Example live test file
├── server.js
└── ...

Example JSON Format (livemock/mock1.json):

Structure your live mock JSON files just like your normal quizzes:
JSON

{
  "title": "Live Biology Assessment 1",
  "questions": [
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "question": "Which organelle is known as the powerhouse of the cell?",
      "options": [
        "Nucleus",
        "Mitochondria",
        "Ribosome",
        "Endoplasmic Reticulum"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "question": "What is the chemical formula of water?",
      "options": [
        "CO2",
        "H2O",
        "NaCl",
        "O2"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    }
  ]
}

When you type mock1 into the Test ID field on your admin-live.html dashboard, the server will automatically look for and read livemock/mock1.json.

from where students will enter the live mock?

Students will enter the live mock test by navigating to the dedicated live test page URL in their web browser:

👉 [https://pioneersprep.in/livetest.html](https://pioneersprep.in/livetest.html) (or http://localhost:3000/livetest.html if you are testing locally).
What they need to do:

    Open the link above.

    Enter the Test ID (e.g., mock1, which corresponds to your file name inside the livemock/ folder).

    Type their First Name and Last Name (which automatically uppercase).

    Enter the Shared OTP that you (the admin) received via email and shared with them.

    Click Join Test to enter the synchronized live screen, where questions will appear automatically as you click Next on your admin dashboard (admin-live.html).

