generate 30 icse exam oriented mcq of high quality from selica class 10- refraction through lens

1. Which of the following points on the principal axis of a lens allows a ray of light to pass through it undeviated?
A) First principal focus
B) Second principal focus
C) Optical centre
D) Centre of curvature
Answer: C) Optical centre

2. A convex lens acts as a magnifying glass when the object is placed:
A) At 2F1​
B) Between F1​ and 2F1​
C) Between the optical centre and F1​
D) At infinity
Answer: C) Between the optical centre and F1​

3. What is the nature of the image formed by a concave lens for an object placed at any finite distance from it?
A) Real, inverted, and diminished
B) Virtual, erect, and magnified
C) Virtual, erect, and diminished
D) Real, erect, and same size
Answer: C) Virtual, erect, and diminished

4. If the lower half of a convex lens is covered with black opaque paper, how is the image of a distant object affected?
A) Only the upper half of the image is formed
B) Only the lower half of the image is formed
C) The full image is formed, but it is inverted twice
D) The full image is formed, but its intensity is reduced
Answer: D) The full image is formed, but its intensity is reduced

5. For a convex lens, what is the minimum distance between a real object and its real image?
A) f
B) 2f
C) 4f
D) Infinity
Answer: C) 4f

6. The linear magnification (m) of a lens is −1. What does this indicate about the image?
A) Virtual, erect, and same size as the object
B) Real, inverted, and same size as the object
C) Real, inverted, and highly diminished
D) Virtual, erect, and highly magnified
Answer: B) Real, inverted, and same size as the object

7. Where must an object be placed in front of a convex lens to obtain a real, inverted image of the same size?
A) At F1​
B) Between F1​ and 2F1​
C) At 2F1​
D) Beyond 2F1​Answer: C) At 2F1​

8. The power of a lens is −2.0 D. What is the type and focal length of this lens?
A) Convex lens, +50 cm
B) Concave lens, −50 cm
C) Convex lens, +20 cm
D) Concave lens, −20 cm
Answer: B) Concave lens, −50 cm

9. How does the focal length of a convex lens change if it is placed in water instead of air?
A) It decreases
B) It increases
C) It remains the same
D) It becomes infinite
Answer: B) It increases

10. How does the focal length of a lens change if red light is replaced by blue light?
A) Focal length increases
B) Focal length decreases
C) Focal length remains unchanged
D) Focal length becomes negative
Answer: B) Focal length decreases

11. Which lens has a real principal focus?
A) Concave lens
B) Convex lens
C) Both have real foci
D) Neither has a real focus
Answer: B) Convex lens

12. An object is placed at infinity in front of a concave lens. The image is formed at:
A) The optical centre
B) The second principal focus (F2​)
C) The first principal focus (F1​)
D) Infinity
Answer: B) The second principal focus (F2​)

13. In a cinema projector, a convex lens is used to project an image on the screen. Where is the film (object) placed?
A) Between the optical centre and F1​
B) At F1​
C) Between F1​ and 2F1​
D) Beyond 2F1​Answer: C) Between F1​ and 2F1​

14. A ray of light directed towards the first principal focus of a convex lens, after refraction:
A) Passes through the second principal focus
B) Emerges parallel to the principal axis
C) Retraces its path
D) Passes through the optical centre
Answer: B) Emerges parallel to the principal axis

15. Two thin lenses of powers +3.5 D and −1.5 D are placed in contact. What is the focal length of the combination?
A) +20 cm
B) +50 cm
C) −50 cm
D) +100 cm
Answer: B) +50 cm

16. Which of the following lenses acts as a diverging lens?
A) Plano-convex lens
B) Concavo-convex lens (thicker at the centre)
C) Double concave lens
D) Biconvex lens
Answer: C) Double concave lens

17. If the linear magnification of an image is positive, the image must be:
A) Real and inverted
B) Virtual and inverted
C) Real and erect
D) Virtual and erect
Answer: D) Virtual and erect

18. A "thick" convex lens compared to a "thin" convex lens (made of the same material) has:
A) Greater focal length and lesser power
B) Lesser focal length and greater power
C) Equal focal length and power
D) Lesser focal length and lesser power
Answer: B) Lesser focal length and greater power

19. Which formula correctly represents the lens formula?
A) v1​+u1​=f1​
B) v1​−u1​=f1​
C) u1​−v1​=f1​
D) v+u=fAnswer: B) v1​−u1​=f1​

20. A student holds a lens close to a printed page and notices that the letters appear upright and magnified. What type of lens is it?
A) Concave lens
B) Convex lens
C) Cylindrical lens
D) Plano-concave lens
Answer: B) Convex lens

21. Where should an object be placed in front of a convex lens so that the image is formed at infinity?
A) At the optical centre
B) At the first principal focus (F1​)
C) At 2F1​
D) Between F1​ and 2F1​Answer: B) At the first principal focus (F1​)

22. A lens is used to correct short-sightedness (myopia). The linear magnification produced by this lens for a real object is always:
A) Greater than 1
B) Equal to 1
C) Less than 1
D) Infinity
Answer: C) Less than 1 (Concave lens always produces diminished images)

23. The SI unit of power of a lens is:
A) Metre
B) Centimetre
C) Dioptre
D) Watt
Answer: C) Dioptre

24. For a concave lens, the first principal focus (F1​) is located:
A) On the side of the incident light
B) On the side of the refracted light
C) At the optical centre
D) At infinity
Answer: B) On the side of the refracted light

25. When sunlight is focused by a convex lens on a piece of paper, the paper burns. The point where the light focuses is the:
A) Optical centre
B) First principal focus
C) Second principal focus
D) Centre of curvature
Answer: C) Second principal focus

26. If an object is placed beyond 2F1​ of a convex lens, the image is formed:
A) Between F2​ and 2F2​, real and diminished
B) Beyond 2F2​, real and magnified
C) At F2​, real and point-sized
D) Between F1​ and optical centre, virtual and erect
Answer: A) Between F2​ and 2F2​, real and diminished

27. A ray of light incident parallel to the principal axis of a concave lens appears to diverge from which point after refraction?
A) Optical centre
B) First principal focus
C) Second principal focus
D) Infinity
Answer: C) Second principal focus

28. According to the New Cartesian Sign Convention, the focal length of a concave lens is always considered:
A) Positive
B) Negative
C) Zero
D) Infinite
Answer: B) Negative

29. The power of a lens is +4.0 D. Its focal length is:
A) +25 cm
B) −25 cm
C) +40 cm
D) +2.5 cm
Answer: A) +25 cm

30. Which of the following factors does the focal length of a lens NOT depend on?
A) Refractive index of the material of the lens
B) Radii of curvature of the two surfaces of the lens
C) Colour of the light used
D) Intensity of the incident light
Answer: D) Intensity of the incident light

